theorem AlgebraicGeometry.WeilGroup.globalSections_eq_invariants.{u} {K : Type u} [Field K] [Finite K]
  {C U : AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme} {p : C ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of K)}
  [AlgebraicGeometry.IsCurve p] {pU : U ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of K)}
  [AlgebraicGeometry.IsCurve pU] {l : ℕ} [Fact (Nat.Prime l)] {W : AlgebraicGeometry.WeilGroup p}
  {V : Type u} [AddCommGroup V] [Module (PadicAlgCl l) V]
  (ρ : Representation (PadicAlgCl l) W.carrier V) {j : U ⟶ C} [AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion j]
  [Nonempty ↥U] {WU : AlgebraicGeometry.WeilGroup pU}
  (R : AlgebraicGeometry.WeilGroup.Restriction j WU W) [FiniteDimensional (PadicAlgCl l) V]
  (_hρ : W.IsLisse l ρ) :
  ∃ e,
    ∀ (f : ↥(W.globalSections l ρ R)),
      e ⟨ρ (R.restrict WU.frobeniusLift) ∘ₗ ↑f, ⋯⟩ = ⟨(ρ (R.restrict WU.frobeniusLift)) ↑(e f), ⋯⟩

AlgebraicGeometry.WeilGroup.IsReal.doc:
Blueprint `sk-d-real-weights`: Local weights and reality.

`ρ` is `ι`-real if `ι P_x(ρ, T)` has real coefficients for every closed point `x`;
equivalently, every complex local eigenvalue multiset is stable under complex conjugation.

